Description: Wild OS Store
 The app store of Wild OS, laid out the way the Microsoft Store is: a home
 page of free apps that replace the ones people used on Windows, browsing by
 category, search that understands Windows app names, and an Installed and
 Updates view.
 .
 Apps come from the Wild OS package repositories through PackageKit and from
 Flathub through libflatpak. Flathub apps install for the signed-in user and
 their sandbox permissions can be changed on the app's page.
